### KAFKA COMMAND USED IN PROJECT ###

1. Generate Cluster ID (KRaft Mode)
    Used once when setting up Kafka.
    bin\windows\kafka-storage.bat random-uuid

2. Format Kafka Storage
    Used only the first time (or after deleting KafkaData).
    bin\windows\kafka-storage.bat format -t CLUSTER_ID -c config\kraft\server.properties

3. Start Kafka Broker
    bin\windows\kafka-server-start.bat config\kraft\server.properties
    Purpose:
    Starts Kafka
    Opens port 9092
    Loads topics and offsets

4. Create Topic
    bin\windows\kafka-topics.bat --create --topic notification-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

5. List Topics
    bin\windows\kafka-topics.bat --list --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

6. Describe Topic
    Shows partitions, replicas, offsets.
    bin\windows\kafka-topics.bat --describe --topic notification-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

7. Delete Topic
    bin\windows\kafka-topics.bat --delete --topic notification-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

8. Start Console Producer
    Send messages manually.
    bin\windows\kafka-console-producer.bat --topic notification-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092
    Then type:
    {"userId":1,"title":"Welcome","message":"Welcome"}

9. Start Console Consumer
    Read messages manually.
    bin\windows\kafka-console-consumer.bat --topic notification-topic --from-beginning --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

10. Read Only New Messages
    bin\windows\kafka-console-consumer.bat --topic notification-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

11. Show Consumer Groups
    bin\windows\kafka-consumer-groups.bat --list --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

12. Describe Consumer Group
    Very important for interviews.
    bin\windows\kafka-consumer-groups.bat --describe --group notification-group --bootstrap-server localhost:9092
    Shows:
    TOPIC
    PARTITION
    CURRENT-OFFSET
    LOG-END-OFFSET
    LAG

13. Reset Consumer Offset
    Move consumer to beginning.
    bin\windows\kafka-consumer-groups.bat ^
    --group notification-group --topic notification-topic --reset-offsets --to-earliest --execute --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

14. Check Broker API Versions
    bin\windows\kafka-broker-api-versions.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

15. Check Metadata Quorum (KRaft)
    Useful in KRaft mode.
    bin\windows\kafka-metadata-quorum.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 describe --status
